#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Oracle-against-Blaze matrix for query, cquery and aquery output formats and flags.

usage: scripts/query/compare --binary PATH --label NAME [--project P[,P...]]
                             [--command query,cquery,aquery] [--cells REGEX] [--no-run]
                             [--details N]
       scripts/query/compare cells [--project P] [--command C]   list the matrix, run nothing
       scripts/query/compare help

Projects: brotli, re2 (copies of the read-only checkouts in ~/.cache/blaze/corpus), probe (a
small generated workspace with select()s, package groups and odd characters), workerd (a sample
of cells through scripts/workerd/run, read-only use). Default: brotli,re2,probe.

Each cell is one command line (expression x --output x flags). For every cell:
  oracle A   the oracle (~/.cache/blaze/oracle/bazel-9.3.2-linux-x86_64) in one server
  oracle B   the oracle again after `shutdown` (a new JVM): Bazel's own run-to-run variation
             (identity hash order in Digraph, HashSet<Target>) shows up as A != B
  blaze      the binary under test
Workspaces: ~/.cache/blaze/work/query-cmp/{o,b}/<project> (rsync of the checkout minus bazel-*
and .git, refreshed at the start of a run); output user roots ~/.cache/blaze/oracle-out/qc-{o,b}.
The two sides' paths have equal lengths, and Blaze's workspace, output base and install base are
replaced by the oracle's in Blaze's stdout (byte for byte, so binary protos stay comparable).
workerd uses its own copies (scripts/workerd/run); its paths are replaced as text only.

Verdict per cell:
  identical            same exit code and same stdout bytes as oracle A or B
  identical-unordered  the oracle itself varies (A != B), or the cell's order comes from Java
                       identity hashes (see order_is_identity_hashed); Blaze's lines (and the
                       items of a factored graph node) equal A's as a multiset
  loud                 Blaze stopped at an `unported!` ("not ported yet") or panicked
  different            anything else (stdout or exit code differ)
Results: ~/.cache/blaze/query-compare/<label>/{results.json,matrix.md,cells/<id>/...}.
--no-run re-classifies the saved outputs. Run it under systemd-run (AGENTS.md: heavy jobs).
"""
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import time

